        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koey/{size}/2187_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-05-02T17:36:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"j1hopki1\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/58f4c7/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> j1hopki1:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It sounds like you didn't make any rule errors. That's sometimes a reason a new villain cleans your clock.Rook City really doesn't help. That place is a ****hole.I would like to note that AZ should not be doing much healing against either Baron Blade. He ramps up fast. This ain't no Dawn fight. AZ should tear through his 29 HP, dealing it right back to Blade. If you do that then Tempest and Legacy would only need to deal around 40 to win.Cosmic Omnitron is just hard. It is one of the few villains that is harder with 5 heroes than with 3. I have a short guide to beating it here:<a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/seek-help-vs-cosmic-omnitron-2937Someone\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/seek-help-vs-cosmic-omnitron-29…</a> mentioned I should put guides in their own thread. I think I might do that. Overall I love the promo villains.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Thanks for the suggestion.</p>\n<p>I figured that much, gonna give MBB another shot in a more neutral environment.</p>\n<p>The first game I got coolant blast out and was able to trade with Baron Blade fast. Which is why I tried the healing approach next.</p>\n<p>I think the fact I had Rook City didn't help.</p>\n<p>I guess I should try keeping Omnitron on side A when I can, but the fact all components blow up kinda makes it hard &gt;&lt;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
